.claude/settings.local.json
.DS_Store

# Only the fictional onboarding profiles live in the tree. A real profile is
# brand data, not project data: it belongs outside the repo, pointed at by
# BRAND_PROFILES_DIR (see CLAUDE.md → "Dónde vive un perfil real").
#
# Do NOT add `!profiles/<brand>/` here to track a real profile. That negation
# is how real brand data got committed to this public repo; the commit gate
# now rejects it (scripts/validate_commit_guardian.py).
profiles/*
!profiles/example/
!profiles/example-personal/

# Reels engine spike (ACU-74). Untracked on purpose — it still has brand
# literals baked in and hasn't been ported to system/ yet — but it is the ONLY
# copy of that work, so it is listed here to keep `git clean -fd` from
# deleting it. Backup: ~/respaldos/prototipo-reel-<fecha>/
prototipo-reel/

# Node / IG carousel generator (system/ig-carousel)
node_modules/
dist/
__pycache__/
system/ig-carousel/output/
system/ig-carousel/week-input.json

# Rendered output of the template profiles (regenerated on demand).
profiles/example/outputs/
profiles/example-personal/outputs/

# Planning notes for the reel/skills separation. Untracked on purpose: the
# document argues about a *specific* brand's leak, so it names that brand,
# its API host and its city throughout. It was written to be read next to the
# work, not published with it.
docs/PLAN-skills-agnosticas.md

# Cached OpenStreetMap responses (system/ig-reel/osm-cache.ts). Never tracked:
# it is a derivative with a TTL, not source, and a blob of a real city's street
# names is dead weight in a public repo that would also age in silence.
#
# Being ignored is also what keeps it out of `--scan`, which walks tracked and
# untracked-but-not-ignored files. Removing this line would make the auditor
# read cached street names as a brand leak.
.cache/

# Términos vigilados que no pueden viajar al repo público (ver
# scripts/brand-denylist.txt y manual_terms() en el validador). Nunca trackeado:
# publicar un denylist es publicar la lista de lo que se quiso ocultar.
scripts/brand-denylist.local.txt

# Borradores de contenido de una persona real (briefs con audiencia, objetivo,
# CTA y posicionamiento). docs/public-repo-rules.md los prohíbe explícitamente:
# "real drafts for a specific person", "local working cards", "content
# describing a real person's audience, objectives, voice, CTA, or positioning".
docs/pi-local-card-*.md

# app/: artefactos de build y copias generadas. Sin esto un `cargo build`
# ensucia el repo con el target de Rust y el proyecto generado por Tauri.
app/src/core/
app/src-tauri/target/
app/src-tauri/gen/
